The phonotactic rules in CLL are neither completely consistent nor complete=
ly=20
clear. xorxes and I, who have both done significant work on the problem,=20
disagree in various details.

For the start of a fu'ivla, I accept any cluster such that all pairs are=20
initially permissible, including arbitrarily long sequences of "st". xorxes=
=20
has a list of three letter sequences. I don't remember them all, but I=20
know "jgl" is one (jglandi=3Dwalnut).

Within a fu'ivla, xorxes accepts anything that can be broken into syllables=
,=20
whatever he allows for syllables, and doesn't contain forbidden substrings=
=20
such as "mz" or "ntc". He accepts "fasxolarto" but not "fasxolarkto". This=
=20
puts him at odds with nitcion, who prefers "fasxolarkto", as it's obvious t=
o=20
him from that spelling that it's a mammal (koala to be precise), not a bake=
d=20
good. I originally wrote "fasxolarto", thinking that "rkt" cannot occur in =
a=20
fu'ivla.

I accept cmevla like "mkparks", where all consonant pairs are valid but not=
=20
initially valid, but I don't think I've figured out how long they can get.=
=20
I'm not sure what xorxes accepts.

Pierre

